loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?C\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u65294 ?}{\uc1 \u22806 ?}{\uc1 \u37096 ?}{\uc1 \u36890 ?}{\uc1 \u20449 ?}{\uc1 \u29615 ?}{\uc1 \u22659 ?}{\uc1 \u35843 ?}{\uc1 \u30740 ?} \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?D{\uc1 \u65294 ?}{\uc1 \u25968 ?}{\uc1 \u25454 ?}{\uc1 \u27969 ?}{\uc1 \u21521 ?}{\uc1 \u22270 ?}{\uc1 \u20998 ?}{\uc1 \u26512 ?}}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?The Rational Unified Process (RUP) is a software engineering process, which captures many of best practices in modem software development. The notions of}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?71 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 and scenarios have been proven to be an excellent way to capture function requirements. RUP can be described in two dimensions - time and content. In the time dimension, the software lifecycle is broken into cycles. Each cycle is divided into four consecutive}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?72 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 which is concluded with a well-defined}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?73 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 and can be further broken down into}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?74 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 - a complete development loop resulting in a release of an executable product, a subset of the final product under development, which grows incrementally to become the final system. The content structure refers to the disciplines, which group}{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?75 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 logically by nature.}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 71\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u12289 ?} A. artifacts \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?B. use-cases \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? C. actors \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? D. workers}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 72\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u12289 ?} A. orientations \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? B. views \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?C. aspects \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?D. phases}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 73\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u12289 ?} A. milestone \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? B. end-mark \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? C. measure \uc1 \u160 ? D. criteria}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 74\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u12289 ?} A. rounds \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? B. loops \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?C. iterations \uc1 \u160 ?D. circularities}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 75\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u12289 ?} A. functions \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? B. workflows \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?C. actions \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u